{The Immortal Zugzwang Game. Nimzowitsch, the author of My System, wins by taking away every useful move White has, until White must lose material to move at all. Move list checked against Wikipedia.}
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. Nc3 O-O 7. O-O d5 8. Ne5 c6 9. cxd5 cxd5 10. Bf4 a6 11. Rc1 b5 12. Qb3 Nc6 13. Nxc6 Bxc6 14. h3 Qd7 15. Kh2 Nh5 16. Bd2 f5 {Black takes space on the kingside and fixes the e4 square.} 17. Qd1 b4 18. Nb1 Bb5 {The bishop takes the e2 square and the f1 rook's file.} 19. Rg1 Bd6 20. e4 fxe4 21. Qxh5 Rxf2 {A rook for the knight, and now every white piece is tied to something.} 22. Qg5 Raf8 23. Kh1 R8f5 24. Qe3 Bd3 {The queen has no squares.} 25. Rce1 h6 {The zugzwang move. Sämisch resigned: every white move loses material.} 0-1
